# TEXT: string ordering. §12 B-11 says byte-lexicographic. Measured on a
# SINGLE comparison it is: "Z" sorts below "a", and a prefix sorts below its
# extension. The non-ASCII row is where it breaks — 0xC3 must sort ABOVE
# 0x7A under unsigned byte order, and it does not, which is what a signed
# char comparison does.
# expect: 1 1 1
# @corpus current
p = "Z"
q = "a"
a = 0
if p < q
    a = 1
r = "ab"
s = "abc"
b = 0
if r < s
    b = 1
t = "\xc3\xa9"
u = "z"
c = 0
if t < u
    c = 1
print("{a} {b} {c}")
